# 🔬 Mini Project 2: Comprehensive Disease Gene Analysis (TP53)

An integrated, end-to-end transcriptomic and proteomic workflow analyzing the structural, evolutionary, and network biology of the human tumor suppressor gene **TP53**—the *"Guardian of the Genome."* 

This project demonstrates how microscopic sequence variations ripple outward to alter structural domains, disrupt biological circuits, and drive clinical cancer pathologies.

---

## 🎯 Project Core Objectives
*   **Pipeline Integration**: Chain multiple foundational bioinformatics platforms (NCBI, UniProt, BLAST, Clustal Omega, InterPro, Pfam, STRING) into a single analytical workflow.
*   **Structural & Evolutionary Mapping**: Track sequence conservation across deep geological time scales and map key functional protein zones.
*   **Biological Data Interpretation**: Transition from simply collecting data rows to analyzing biological circuits, explaining the molecular mechanisms behind clinical cancer mutations.

